6. FULL JENSEN THRESHOLD SUM
================================================================================
  Following S71 / S72 convention:
  delta(1/g_i^2)(tau) = sum_{(p,q) != (0,0)} T_i(p,q)/(8 pi^2)
                       * ln(Lambda_R^2 / omega_{eff}(p,q)^2)
                       * exp(-omega_{eff}^2 / Lambda_R^2)
  where omega_{eff}(p,q) is the per-sector effective mass.
  W2-J refinement over S72/S71:
    - We use three choices for omega_eff:
      (I)  omega_min(p,q)                -- S71 convention, S_inf = 2.353
      (II) <omega>(p,q)                 -- arithmetic mean over the sector
      (III) per-mode average of ln(Lambda/omega_k) -- full Jensen resolution
    - Jensen dependence enters through omega_min, <omega>, {omega_k}
      (all already baked into the W1-C cache at tau = 0.19).

  Lambda_cut = 1.001 * max(omega) = 4.3004 M_KK units
  Regulator: Gaussian  f(omega/Lambda_R) = exp(-(omega/Lambda_R)^2)
    Lambda_R = 2.0480 M_KK (from S71 spectral zeta threshold)

