7. BI-INVARIANT (tau = 0) LIMIT -- analytic cross-check
================================================================================
  At tau = 0 the Jensen deformation is absent.  The eigenvalues of D_K on
  the round SU(3) take values |lambda_{(p,q)}| = sqrt(C_2(p,q) + C_2(Spin)).
  Without per-mode splitting, log(Lambda/omega) is common to every mode in
  a sector, so the Jensen-dressed sum degenerates to the UNIVERSAL S72 model
  with the simple ratio
     delta_i / delta_3 = T_i^{tot} / T_3^{tot}
  where T_i^{tot} = sum_sectors T_i(p,q) * n_modes(p,q) / dim(p,q)
  This is the limit that S72 Model A (universal) was approximating.
  T_1^tot (GUT-normalized): 954086.4000
  T_2^tot                : 132512.0000
  T_3^tot                : 132512.0000
  T_1^tot / T_3^tot      : 7.2000
  T_2^tot / T_3^tot      : 1.0000
  (Compare S72 Model A: delta_i / delta_3 = 1:1:1 assumed universal.)

